Data
====

Food composition data (app/src/main/assets/food/foods.tsv and recipes.tsv), built by tools/food-db; sources and changes
are described in docs/third-party/food-data/README.md:

  - USDA FoodData Central (Foundation Foods 2026-04, SR Legacy 2018-04, FNDDS 2019-2020): public domain,
    CC0 1.0. U.S. Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Research Service. FoodData Central, 2019.
    fdc.nal.usda.gov.
  - Ciqual 2025 food composition table: Etalab Open Licence 2.0. Anses. 2025. Table de composition
    nutritionnelle des aliments Ciqual (version of 2025-11-03). https://ciqual.anses.fr/
  - Open Food Facts (looked up online for barcodes, not bundled): Open Database License (ODbL 1.0),
    https://world.openfoodfacts.org


Food recognition models
=======================

app/src/main/assets/food/food_model.tflite (food classifier with a grams-estimate head) and
food_detector.tflite (food-item detector) are our own models, trained with the scripts in tools/food-model/
(see tools/food-model/MODEL_CARD.md).

- The classifier starts from the ImageNet-12k/1k weights of MobileNetV4-Conv-Medium by timm
  (https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models, Apache-2.0; architecture by Google). Its grams head
  is calibrated on Nutrition5k (Google, CC BY 4.0, https://github.com/google-research-datasets/Nutrition5k).
- The detector is Ultralytics YOLO11n (Copyright Ultralytics, AGPL-3.0, https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics),
  fine-tuned from its COCO weights.
- Both were trained on photos from Open Images V7 (Google LLC; annotations and boxes CC BY 4.0, images listed
  as CC BY 2.0 by their Flickr authors), from Wikimedia Commons (CC0, public domain, CC BY and CC BY-SA files,
  each by its author; classifier only) and from the MyFoodRepo / AIcrowd Food Recognition Benchmark 2022
  (CC BY 4.0, Mohanty et al., Frontiers in Nutrition 2022).

docs/third-party/food-model/ names every photo used, with its author, licence and source page. The
photos themselves are not distributed.


